  Final Answer:                                                                                                                          
  As a Senior QA Test Case Engineer, I have analyzed the reported issue (BUG-1024). Given that the system returns a 500 Internal Server  
  Error, this indicates a backend failure during the order processing transaction when a coupon entity is involved.                      
                                                                                                                                         
  Below is the structured test suite designed to validate the fix and ensure comprehensive coverage of the checkout/payment              
  integration.                                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                                         
  ### Test Case Suite: Checkout Coupon Processing                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                         
  | TC ID | Req Ref | Title | Preconditions | Test Data | Test Steps | Expected Result | Type | Priority | Coverage |                    
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |                                                                
  | **TC-001** | BUG-1024 | Verify successful order placement with a valid discount coupon | User logged in, items in cart | Valid       
  Coupon Code (e.g., "SAVE10") | 1. Add items to cart. 2. Apply coupon. 3. Proceed to checkout. 4. Click "Place Order". | Order placed   
  successfully; redirect to confirmation page. | Functional | Critical | Positive |                                                      
  | **TC-002** | BUG-1024 | Verify 500 error does not occur when placing order without a coupon | User logged in, items in cart | N/A |  
  1. Add items to cart. 2. Proceed to checkout without coupon. 3. Click "Place Order". | Order processed successfully. | Regression |    
  High | Positive |                                                                                                                      
  | **TC-003** | BUG-1024 | Validate handling of expired or invalid coupons | User logged in | Expired/Fake Coupon Code | 1. Apply       
  invalid coupon. 2. Proceed to checkout. 3. Click "Place Order". | Appropriate error message shown; order blocked or processed at full  
  price (depending on business rule). No 500 error. | Negative | Medium | Boundary |                                                     
  | **TC-004** | BUG-1024 | Verify coupon calculation logic on backend | User logged in | Coupon with percentage/fixed discount | 1.     
  Apply coupon. 2. Observe cart totals. 3. Place order. | Calculated totals match backend transaction logs; no 500 error. | Business     
  Rules | High | Functional |                                                                                                            
  | **TC-005** | BUG-1024 | Test checkout with maximum allowed discount items | User logged in | Multi-item cart | 1. Apply coupon. 2.   
  Add multiple units of high-value items. 3. Click "Place Order". | Order processes successfully; discount applied correctly to          
  subtotal. | Edge Case | High | Boundary |                                                                                              
  | **TC-006** | BUG-1024 | Validate input sanitization for coupon field | User logged in | Malicious string (e.g., `<script>`) | 1.     
  Enter script in coupon field. 2. Attempt to apply. 3. Proceed to checkout. | System rejects input/no exception triggered; no 500       
  error. | Negative | High | Security |                                                                                                  
  | **TC-007** | BUG-1024 | Verify session integrity during coupon application | User logged in | Valid coupon | 1. Apply coupon. 2.     
  Refresh browser. 3. Attempt to place order. | Coupon remains applied; order processes without 500 error. | Functional | Medium |       
  Regression |                                                                                                                           
  | **TC-008** | BUG-1024 | Verify database/transaction rollback on failed payment with coupon | User logged in | Valid coupon, Invalid  
  payment method | 1. Apply coupon. 2. Enter invalid card details. 3. Attempt to place order. | Transaction gracefully rejected; error   
  message displayed; no partial/orphaned order created. | Error Handling | High | Negative |                                             
                                                                                                                                         
  ---                                                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                         
  ### Coverage Analysis Summary:                                                                                                         
  *   **Positive Scenarios:** Validates that the happy path is restored (TC-001, TC-002).                                                
  *   **Negative/Boundary:** Ensures invalid inputs or edge case math logic don't trigger server-side crashes (TC-003, TC-005, TC-006).  
  *   **Error Handling:** Confirms that if a failure occurs (e.g., payment failure), the system handles it gracefully rather than        
  throwing a 500 status (TC-008).                                                                                                        
  *   **Regression:** Ensures that standard checkout functionality (without coupons) remains stable and that session state persists      
  correctly (TC-002, TC-007).                                                                                                            
  *   **Business Logic:** Verifies that the interaction between the discounting engine and the order placement service is synchronized   
  (TC-004).                                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                         


